-04f9363f618a" 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431904 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431905 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431907 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431910 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431912 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431923 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431923 1077 "selection" 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431923 1078 #edb/ref 17592186431904 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431923 1079 #uuid "ee4e4c14-1eab-5c99-a4c6-676aa4a2d4a3" 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431924 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431921 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431924 1069 "q-183358" 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431924 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431924 1071 "Consider the following predicates.\n\n$\\,$ $A(x):$ $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}.$ $\\,$ $B(x):$ $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$ \n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the biconditional predicate $A(x)⇔B(x)?$\n\nI. $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ if and only if $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$\n\nII. If $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ then $x\\in {Z}^{-},$ or if $x\\in {Z}^{-}$ then $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}.$\n\nIII. $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ is equivalent to  $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$" 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431924 1072 #uuid "0af36684-2b78-59f1-bddf-9a1297846d8d" 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431924 1074 "A biconditional expression $P⇔Q≡(P⇒Q)∧(Q⇒P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A⇔B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ if and only if $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$\n\n- $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ is equivalent to  $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$\n\n- If $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ then $x\\in {Z}^{-},$ and if $x\\in {Z}^{-}$ then $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431925 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431922 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431925 1069 "q-183377" 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431925 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431925 1071 "Find the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the universal set $R:$\n\n- $P(x):$ $3x-1<5$\n\n- $Q(x):$ ${x}^{2}<4$" 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431925 1072 #uuid "4998a63e-08c3-54c9-83d8-95967f9e62e0" 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431925 1074 "Since we have that\n\n$$\nP(x)⇔Q(x)≡(P(x)∧Q(x))∨(¬P(x)∧¬Q(x)),\n$$\n\n \n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇔Q}=({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- To find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-1 & <5 \\\\ 3x & <6 \\\\ x & <2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is\n${T}_{P}=(-\\infty ,2).$\nAs a result, the complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}=[2,\\infty ).$\n\n- To find the the truth set of $Q(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & <4 \\\\ -2 & <x<2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n${T}_{Q}=(-2,2)$ \nand its complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}=(-\\infty ,-2]\\cup [2,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q} & =(-\\infty ,2)\\cap (-2,2) \\\\  & =(-2,2) \\\\ {\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q} & =[2,\\infty )\\cap ((-\\infty ,-2]\\cup [2,\\infty )) \\\\  & =[2,\\infty ) \\\\ {T}_{P⇔Q} & =({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}) \\\\  & =(-2,2)\\cup [2,\\infty ) \\\\  & =(-2,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431926 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431923 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431926 1069 "q-183352" 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431926 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431926 1071 "$\\,$ If $x>2,$ then ${x}^{3}>3.$\n\nWhich of the following is logically equivalent to the conditional predicate above?" 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431926 1072 #uuid "7f523a19-f527-5654-8f5b-d082a72f3c43" 13194139534669 17592186045417 true] [17592186431926 1074 "Let's denote by $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x>2.$\n\n- $Q(x):$ ${x}^{3}>3.$\n\nThen, our initial sentence can be written as $P(x)⇒Q(x),$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬P(x)∨Q(x).\n$$\n\nThe negation of $P(x)$ can be written as\n\n- $¬P(x):$ $x\\le 2.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x\\le 2,$ or ${x}^{3}>3.$" 13194139534669 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0257e9ae-233c-5479-a73a-f7d15634f050" 17592186431891 "answer-09cfb0bd-16fc-5ff8-83ea-181ccaa5b830" 17592186431892 "answer-0f3520f9-b73e-5970-b706-b9779285c6d8" 17592186431893 "answer-15712b1e-16bc-5a53-a8f5-faa576334228" 17592186431894 "answer-172c866e-61d5-5acd-a888-4900172f90ee" 17592186431895 "answer-1f2ea10d-0ba6-575d-b2b9-4bb8eff6bf56" 17592186431896 "answer-284a22fb-39a1-56ea-a4c8-f426f8726f7e" 17592186431897 "answer-3171c0d3-b6e0-5731-b749-9f6d2eb044fb" 17592186431898 "answer-40aa1415-19a6-5cc1-81a0-34ea36dba726" 17592186431899 "answer-59a9825b-78e1-597e-9ae8-b1be3edf28e4" 17592186431900 "answer-5bf6434d-2d00-5137-9f92-022547235944" 17592186431901 "answer-6068ed92-2671-5bb0-a875-613111bd318c" 17592186431902 "answer-63bac827-f548-588b-9cd2-6ca1551b28ad" 17592186431903 "answer-6a2679c9-621d-544a-a902-796ccdb490cc" 17592186431904 "answer-6da4f59a-b248-5921-ab4d-626912ea5f8f" 17592186431905 "answer-756036f3-c0c0-5c51-aa92-cf3de0e04a2f" 17592186431906 "answer-7fd1c0a7-682a-5848-b7be-27c0eb91c14f" 1759218643